00:34:39,547 --> 00:34:40,707
[SPEAKER_04]: How do you say it?

379
00:34:42,108 --> 00:34:56,371
[SPEAKER_04]: Unrecognizable and so big thing that I hope that you come to the one time to the point where you can understand it.

380
00:34:57,071 --> 00:34:57,831
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that's what I'm saying.

381
00:34:58,452 --> 00:35:08,034
[SPEAKER_00]: You are closer to contemplating death when you are practicing sense restraint than you are when you think about death on the basis of non-sense restraint.

382
00:35:09,747 --> 00:35:20,713
[SPEAKER_00]: So, whether you think about death or not, if you keep the virtue, practice sense restraint, don't act towards sensuality, that is already closer to the contemplation of death, contemplation of cessation.

383
00:35:22,414 --> 00:35:28,738
[SPEAKER_00]: And your idea of contemplation, if it's based on the non-restraint, non-virtue, it's not actually that close.

384
00:35:28,858 --> 00:35:32,280
