00:36:50,041 --> 00:36:51,102
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, thank you.

400
00:36:51,182 --> 00:37:00,573
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just before I was introduced to Buddhism, I've heard a lot about introspection and very little about contemplation and the terms never connected for me.

401
00:37:00,653 --> 00:37:01,074
[SPEAKER_01]: Right, right.

402
00:37:03,437 --> 00:37:04,498
[SPEAKER_00]: No, definitely, definitely.

403
00:37:04,658 --> 00:37:06,920
[SPEAKER_00]: Contemplation should be a form of introspection.

404
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:07,521
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's say like that.

405
00:37:07,561 --> 00:37:17,370
[SPEAKER_00]: Contemplation should not be just pondering about abstract terms and how they relate in space and time and what the connections are and how they correspond and what are their similarities.

406
00:37:18,170 --> 00:37:22,674
[SPEAKER_00]: Contemplation should be seeing those things introspectively, on the level of... that's what I mean.

407
00:37:22,694 --> 00:37:25,737
[SPEAKER_00]: It needs to be taken personally and seen on that personal level.

